  bodyName: Mercury
  classification: Terrestrial Planet
  positionFromSun: 1st Planet
  overview: 'Mercury is the smallest planet and the closest planet to the Sun.

    It
    has a rocky, heavily cratered surface, a large metallic core

    and an extremely
    thin exosphere. Its surface experiences

    extreme temperature variations
    between day and night.'
  keyCharacteristics: '- Smallest planet in the Solar System.

    - Closest planet
    to the Sun.

    - Heavily cratered surface.

    - Large iron-rich core.

    -
    No known natural satellites.

    - Experiences a 3:2 spin-orbit resonance.'
